#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:2
msgid "``robots.txt`` support"
msgstr "``robots.txt`` 支持"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:4
msgid ""
"The `robots.txt`_ files allow you to customize how your documentation is "
"indexed in search engines. It's useful for:"
msgstr "`robots.txt`_ 文件可让你自定义文档在搜索引擎中的索引方式。它适用于："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:7
msgid "Hiding various pages from search engines"
msgstr "对搜索引擎隐藏特定页面"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:8
msgid "Disabling certain web crawlers from accessing your documentation"
msgstr "禁止特定网络爬虫访问你的文档"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:9
msgid "Disallowing any indexing of your documentation"
msgstr "禁止索引你的文档"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:11
msgid ""
"Read the Docs automatically generates one for you with a configuration that "
"works for most projects. By default, the automatically created "
"``robots.txt``:"
msgstr "Read the Docs 会自动为你生成一份对大多数项目都适用的配置。默认情况下，自动生成的 ``robots.txt`` ："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:14
msgid ""
"Hides versions which are set to :ref:`Hidden <versions:Version states>` from"
" being indexed."
msgstr "隐藏设置为 :ref:`隐藏 <versions:Version states>` 的版本，不使其被索引。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:15
msgid "Allows indexing of all other versions."
msgstr "允许索引所有其他版本。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:19
msgid ""
"``robots.txt`` files are respected by most search engines, but they aren't a"
" guarantee that your pages will not be indexed. Search engines may choose to"
" ignore your ``robots.txt`` file, and index your docs anyway."
msgstr ""
"大多数搜索引擎会遵守 ``robots.txt`` 文件，但这并不保证你的页面不会被索引。搜索引擎可能选择忽略你的 ``robots.txt`` "
"文件，仍然索引你的文档。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:24
msgid ""
"If you require *private* documentation, please see "
":doc:`/commercial/sharing`."
msgstr "如需*私有* 文档，请参阅 :doc:`/commercial/sharing` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:27
msgid "How it works"
msgstr "工作原理"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:29
msgid ""
"You can customize this file to add more rules to it. The ``robots.txt`` file"
" will be served from the **default version** of your project. This is "
"because the ``robots.txt`` file is served at the top-level of your domain, "
"so we must choose a version to find the file in. The **default version** is "
"the best place to look for it."
msgstr ""
"你可以自定义该文件以添加更多规则。``robots.txt`` 文件将从项目的**默认版本** 提供。因为 ``robots.txt`` "
"在域名顶层提供服务，我们必须选择某个版本来查找该文件，** 默认版本** 是最合适的位置。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:36
msgid "Tool integration"
msgstr "工具集成"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:38
msgid ""
"Documentation tools will have different ways of generating a ``robots.txt`` "
"file. We have examples for some of the most popular tools below."
msgstr "不同文档工具生成 ``robots.txt`` 的方式各不相同。下面给出一些最常用工具的示例。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:43
msgid "Sphinx"
msgstr "Sphinx"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:45
msgid ""
"Sphinx uses the `html_extra_path`_ configuration value to add static files "
"to its final HTML output. You need to create a ``robots.txt`` file and put "
"it under the path defined in ``html_extra_path``."
msgstr ""
"Sphinx 使用 `html_extra_path`_ 配置值将静态文件加入最终 HTML 输出。你需要创建 ``robots.txt`` 文件并放到"
" ``html_extra_path`` 定义的路径下。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:48
msgid "MkDocs"
msgstr "MkDocs"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:50
msgid ""
"MkDocs needs the ``robots.txt`` to be at the directory defined by the "
"`docs_dir`_ configuration value."
msgstr "MkDocs 要求 ``robots.txt`` 位于 `docs_dir`_ 配置值定义的目录中。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/robots.rst:58
msgid ":doc:`/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide`"
msgstr ":doc:`/guides/technical-docs-seo-guide`"

